name was intentionally encoded: `# (.bridge_state.bak-retarget) cannot survive by not being named explicitly.`"],"finding":"AC4's consumer-enumeration grep is scoped to `src/ .github/` but misses `tests/`, where `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py` line 47 names `.bridge_state.bak-retarget` as a literal string constant in `_NON_TICKET_ENTRIES`. That set is used by `_tickets_branch_entries()` to filter branch listings during live-Jira store-copy tests. If the directory is deleted and the constant is not updated, the test retains a now-dead entry in its exclusion set — harmless today but wrong, and a signal that the consumer inventory was produced by a hand-scoped grep rather than a full-tree sweep.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd3f87a2560a5b380","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC4: \"`grep -rn 'bak-retarget' src/ .github/` returns no consumer. Tier: grep assertion.\"","norm_id":"nb5e77911b74fa230","priority":0.352,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py` retains `.bridge_state.bak-retarget` in `_NON_TICKET_ENTRIES` after deletion — a stale dead entry that AC4's grep will never catch because `tests/` is outside its scope.","AC4 passes as written even though a real consumer (the test file) was not reviewed, giving a false 'no consumers' verdict."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change AC4 to: `grep -rn 'bak-retarget' src/ .github/ tests/` (or `.` for the full tree). Then remove the literal `\".bridge_state.bak-retarget\"` string from `_NON_TICKET_ENTRIES` in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py` as a companion cleanup in the same commit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a concrete proving command for AC2, e.g.: `git clone --branch tickets <repo> /tmp/fresh-checkout && du -sb /tmp/fresh-checkout | awk '{print $1}'` before and after, asserting the delta is >=33,025,572 bytes (or equivalently `git ls-tree -r --long HEAD tickets | awk 'BEGIN{s=0}{s+=$4}END{print s}'` diff).","cohort":["E2","E6","F1"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 states only 'Tier: repo measurement' with no stated command, no measurement baseline source, and no checkout procedure.","Verify-command defect taxonomy item (4): fixture/protocol not defined — the criterion can be satisfied in multiple non-equivalent ways (du on full worktree, git ls-tree byte sum, git clone + du) with no stated canonical method."],"finding":"AC2 names a >=33 MB checkout-size drop as a completion-relevant criterion but provides no concrete proving command — no tool (`du`, `git ls-files --others`, etc.), no directory target, and no protocol for what constitutes a 'fresh checkout' for measurement purposes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4efb1dd74341c947","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC2: 'Working-tree size of a fresh checkout drops by >=33 MB. Tier: repo measurement.'","norm_id":"n6213e60a24816e6b","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An executing agent measures the wrong directory or uses a cached worktree and gets a misleading reading, leaving the AC unverified despite the deletion being correct.","A reviewer cannot reproduce the measurement because the command and target are unspecified."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Append to AC2: 'Prove with: `git ls-tree -r --long HEAD | grep bak-retarget | awk \"{s+=$4}END{print s}\"` reporting 0 after deletion vs 33,040,758 before (sum from session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4).' This avoids a full clone while giving a deterministic, reproducible byte count.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify in AC3 whether the 'before' diagnostic baseline is (a) the count recorded in session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 (cite it explicitly in the AC) or (b) must be re-measured live before deletion, and if (b), add a prerequisite step 'Run `rebar fsck > /tmp/fsck_before.txt` before any file removal' so the ordering is unambiguous.","cohort":["E2","E6","F1"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3 says 'before and after deletion' — implying two live measurements bracketing the deletion.","'do not re-derive' in the header implies the before-count is already recorded in the session log.","Verify-command defect taxonomy item 7: a command assumes state a prior step must establish — the 'before' count must be captured before the deletion step, but no ordering is stated."],"finding":"AC3 requires a 'before and after' diagnostic multiset comparison, but the plan does not specify whether the 'before' baseline must be captured live (before the deletion is made) or can be taken from session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4. The 'do not re-derive' instruction in the plan header conflicts with the AC's implicit requirement for a live pre-deletion measurement, leaving the sequencing and baseline source ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3bb64bf365ca9bf0","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC3: 'rebar fsck reports the identical diagnostic multiset before and after deletion'; Plan header: 'session_log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 (measured facts; do not re-derive)'.","norm_id":"ne0e3b5e0c74c9921","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An executing agent deletes the directory first and then tries to run the 'before' measurement, which is now impossible, leaving AC3 unprovable.","An agent uses the session-log count as the before-baseline but the plan never explicitly authorizes this, so reviewers dispute whether the baseline is valid."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Revise AC3 to: 'rebar fsck reports the identical diagnostic multiset before and after deletion — use the 561-diagnostic baseline recorded in session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 as the before-count; run `rebar fsck` after deletion and assert the count-by-kind output matches exactly.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an explicit rollback/back-out statement (e.g., 'Back-out: `git revert <deletion-sha>` on the tickets branch; must be executed before epic 0303-692c's history strip runs') to satisfy T4's requirement for a named reversibility mechanism, not just implicit commit reversibility.","cohort":["COH","E1","T4"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["T4 rubric: 'The remedy is an explicit rollback/back-out plan or expand-contract — acknowledgement alone is insufficient'","Plan states 'no history rewrite' (implying plain commit) but never writes: 'Back-out: git revert <sha> on the tickets branch restores the directory before the history strip runs'","The sequencing dependency on epic 0303-692c means a rollback window is implicitly bounded, yet no window or procedure is named"],"finding":"The plan does not include an explicit rollback / back-out procedure for the destructive deletion commit. While the operation is a plain commit (not a history rewrite) and thus implicitly reversible via `git revert`, T4 requires the reversibility mechanism to be stated explicitly — acknowledgement of justif